From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp extras from mastertune: latch, ratchet notes, bounce,
 bounce length and velocity, roll and ball

Ports the arpeggiator additions of mastertune 1.2.1 (its patches 0005, 0006, 0021, 0024, 0117 and 0120) onto v1.3.
mastertune's arp is 1.3's own arp backported, so the engine came over as a three-way merge: v1.3's
arpeggiator with mastertune's code since its backport, keeping what v1.3 added since (the note's sampleSyncLength,
song_firmware_version, the "mode" attribute as 1.3 writes it).

- Latch: the arp keeps playing the notes after the keys are let go; the next key pressed after all were let go
  replaces them without the arp losing time. Switching latch off stops what's latched. Not for a kit row (one note),
  but for the kit arp.
- Ratchet notes: Auto (2, 4 or 8 at random, as 1.3), exactly 2 ... 8, Roll (as many hits as fit until the plates
  close, at least 16 ms apart) or Ball (a ping-pong ball between plates that meet after the first step and part
  again).
- Ratchet bounce -10 ... +10: each gap of a ratchet the one before times r (faster or slower), 0 even as in 1.3.
- Bounce length 1 ... 16: how many arp steps a ratchet lasts.
- Bounce velocity: Even, Fade (softer as the gaps get shorter) or Rise (louder).
- Fixes that came with them: a ratchet's hits that fell behind are dropped rather than pushing the next step back, a
  new step drops what's left of the last step's ratchet, and an arp without settings (an instrument without a clip)
  plays plain notes instead of reading through null.
- Latched notes are dropped once the arp is off (its mode, a preset, or a clip of the instrument without the arp), not
  started as held notes: their keys were let go long before, so nothing would end them. mastertune 1.2.1 has this
  fault (found in the review of this port); on a kit arp switched off it left the latched rows sounding for good.

Menus in the 1.3 style: Latch is a toggle in the arpeggiator menu, after Mode; the four ratchet settings are a new
horizontal menu "Ratchet" after Pattern (synth, kit row, kit arp, MIDI and CV), in the arp's menu group. The settings
are saved as mastertune saves them (latch, ratchetNotes, ratchetBounce, ratchetBounceLength, ratchetBounceFade), so
songs move between mastertune 1.2.1 and this build; stock v1.3 ignores them.
